These files quote text from Wikipedia and Wikisource, or are derived from the
Tajik Shahnameh corpus (ArabovMK/shahnameh-tajik-corpus), and are licensed under
CC BY-SA 4.0 instead (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/):
ezafe-written-dev.jsonl, ezafe-junctions-dev.jsonl, ezafe-lab-1.jsonl,
arabic-spans-lab.jsonl, arabic-lines-lab.jsonl, shahnameh-tajik-test.jsonl.

corpus-sample.jsonl.gz is the Sample tier of the Ghazal Corpus 1.0.0, 500
documents, each under the licence in its own `license` field: CC BY-SA 4.0
(Wikimedia text; its authors are in the history of each document's url), CC0 1.0
(Common Voice) or public domain (Ganjoor poems whose poets died long ago).
corpus-sample.json is its manifest, with the full attribution statement.

verb-stems.tsv and verb-preverbs.tsv include lexical facts checked against
English Wiktionary (Wiktionary contributors, via the Kaikki Persian extract)
and are distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
https://en.wiktionary.org/
https://kaikki.org/dictionary/Persian/
Dehkhoda infinitive entries were also consulted for stem facts; no dictionary
definitions or corpus passages are reproduced in these tables.
